# Activities pinned away from their maturity default, each with its reason. Most move
# earlier. A few move later, where the work cannot start until the fleet integrates.
# Early pins also cover what the interim authorization to test needs in Phase 1, and
# fleet work proven on the spare stations and the simulator before the fleet integrates.
# A few move from Phase 1 to Phase 2 where they cannot be used before then, which keeps
# Phase 1 to the foundation.
# Level 2 defaults to Phase 2 at the earliest and Level 3 to Phase 4. A pin is
# used only where KESTREL's design depends on the activity from the start, or
# where building it in costs far less than retrofitting it.
